        a                       ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment            "Middle East, Textile; Dress fabric of woven silk and metal thread, Iran, 1800-1870"@en , "Dress fabric of woven silk and metal thread.\n\nWoven silk and metal thread, plain weave ground.\nWarp: pink silk, indeterminable twist.\nWeft: white, blue, black and red silk, all indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk core, Z-twist.\n\nIncomplete pattern on a yellow ground which was originally metal thread but has worn. There is an 8-petalled flower form in white edged in black, each lobe containing a stylised blue blossom emerging from behind and 8-pointed star, again in white edged in black, with a central infill of a rosette with heart-shaped petals in red with a blue and yellow centre. Around the main rosette form are indications of other flower forms in white edged in black and linked to each other by a blue flower; sprays of red buds cover the ground."@en ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note        "Middle East, Textile; Dress fabric of woven silk and metal thread, Iran, 1800-1870"@en , "Dress fabric of woven silk and metal thread.\n\nWoven silk and metal thread, plain weave ground.\nWarp: pink silk, indeterminable twist.\nWeft: white, blue, black and red silk, all indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk core, Z-twist.\n\nIncomplete pattern on a yellow ground which was originally metal thread but has worn. There is an 8-petalled flower form in white edged in black, each lobe containing a stylised blue blossom emerging from behind and 8-pointed star, again in white edged in black, with a central infill of a rosette with heart-shaped petals in red with a blue and yellow centre. Around the main rosette form are indications of other flower forms in white edged in black and linked to each other by a blue flower; sprays of red buds cover the ground."@en ;
